<p>I'm always very excited to announce a new website. Actually, the reason this exists is because of my dissatisfaction with Itch.io for the distribution of <i><a href="https://blackmagicblues.itch.io/black-magic-blues">Black Magic Blues</a></i>. I don't have anything against Itch - in fact, I've used plenty it in the past for distributing smaller PDFs, such as my tabletop games work and my first [aborted] webcomic. Itch is quite good in the former case, but it's mainly because of the culture that has sprung up around TTRPG distribution on Itch, meaning that indie TTRPG fans are incentivized to stick around and learn the "grammar" of Itch.</p>
<p>When it comes to comics, though, there's two downsides, one of which is more obvious. The obvious one is that comics distributed via Itch must be "finished" comics, or at least can't be ongoing, unless the author wants to continually update the PDF on the Itch page every time they finish an update. The second is simply that comics are not (quite) as niche as TTRPGs, and so there is too much friction for would-be readers who don't use Itch, and no comparable culture to incentivize them to figure it out.</p>
<p>Of course, there are plenty of other options for hosting comics - Webtoons and Tapas for hosting on other people's domains; Comicfury et al. for hosting on your own domain [sort of]. I'm not that keen on the former because I simply don't like the format; on the latter, because I'm vain.</p>
<p>In the hopes of creating a more frictionless reading experience, I've put together this site. I don't expect I'll change too much about the site's design from here, but small things may change here and there, especially if they concern accessibility, a cause that's always been near to my heart.</p>
<p>Anyway, this being the inaugural post, that means chapter 1 is also finished and uploaded! I considered rambling on about every little detail, but I think the less I say about it, the better. All I'll say is that <i>IA IA IA</i> is an intentional break with <i>Black Magic Blues</i>. I of course enjoy writing about Jangrel Plonks, and imagine I'll return to him sooner or later, but writing <i>Final Fantasy XIV</i> fan comics was never my full ambition.</p>
<p>Please enjoy the first chapter of <i>IA IA IA</i>.</p>